# Netlify serves every first-party asset as `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# by default, because the filenames are not fingerprinted. ETags mean repeat
# visitors get 304s rather than re-downloads, so the cost is a conditional
# round trip per asset per visit — about ten of them, which is noticeable on
# mobile.
#
# NOTE ON `immutable`: these filenames are NOT content-hashed. `immutable` with
# a one-year max-age would make a stale asset unfixable without renaming the
# file, so the asset directories get one week instead. /vendor/ IS effectively
# immutable — every file there carries its exact upstream version in the name
# (react-18.3.1..., leaflet-1.9.4...) and a version bump changes the filename —
# so it gets the full year.
#
# HTML stays uncached so content and CMS-driven markup update immediately.
# Netlify already sets HSTS.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN

/vendor/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/static/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/index.html
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
